hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4326","The narrator named Yahya has reported this, and the woman named Umrah has narrated: Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned this to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: This should not prevent you; buy her and set her free, for the right of wala’ belongs to the one who sets free. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This is the last part of the collection of various types of commands transmitted from the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). We have mentioned these commands under chapters and sub-divisions. Now, some hadiths from the commands remain, which we have transmitted in various places among other types, because they are more suitable for those places, just as we have transmitted some of these hadiths under the commands as well, so that the purpose regarding this may be achieved. After this, we will dictate the second type, which relates to prohibitions. We will mention it under various chapters and sub-divisions, just as we dictated the commands, if Allah Almighty so decides and wills. May Allah Almighty include us among those who, when stating rulings about Allah’s religion, remain detached from the desires of those who are excessive, and do not follow the opinions of those who pursue perverse desires and evil views in new issues. Indeed, He (that is, Allah Almighty) is the best to be asked."
"4327","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever attributes himself to anyone other than his emancipator, let him prepare for his special place in Hell."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Hisn is Hisn bin Abdur Rahman Taraghami. He belonged to the people of Damascus and he is the grandfather of Salamah bin Ayyar. Besides this narration, two other hadiths are also transmitted from him."
"4328","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, 'Which of the people are best?' He said: 'My generation, then those that follow them, then those that follow them. Then there will come people whose testimony precedes their oath and whose oath precedes their testimony.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2362)"
"4329","I love you people."
"4330","“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The likeness of this world in comparison to the Hereafter is that of anyone of you dipping his finger into the sea: let him see what he brings forth.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4108)"
"4331","I said: You have spoken the truth, but I only leave out your name. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What is your opinion about this: If you camp in a valley where there are many trees from which (animals) have eaten, and there you find a tree from which nothing has been eaten, where would you let your camel graze? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: By the tree from which nothing has been eaten. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) meant: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not marry any virgin woman other than her."
"4332","narrates: Whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would take an oath, he would use these words: ""By the One who turns the hearts."
"4333","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) has narrated this, that the Messenger of Allah said: What is meant by it is a person saying: ""No, by Allah! Yes, by Allah!"
"4334","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Allah has forgiven my nation for what they think of to themselves, so long as they do not act upon it or speak of it."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2040)"
"4335","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Allah has forgiven my nation for what they think of to themselves, so long as they do not act upon it or speak of it."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2040)"
"4336","""Eisa bin Maryam saw a man stealing and said: 'Did you steal?' He said: 'No, by the One besides Whom there is no other God.' 'Eisa said: 'I believe in Allah, and I do not believe what my eyes see.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2102)"
"4337","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: But only one woman gave birth to an incomplete child. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If he had said 'InshaAllah' at that time, it would have happened as he had stated."
"4338","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: If he had said 'InshaAllah', he would not have broken his oath and his wish would have been fulfilled."
"4339","The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone says when swearing an oath: ""If Allah wills,"" he makes an exception. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3261)"
"4340","'Whoever swears an oath and says In sha' Allah, he will have made an exception.""(2) (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2104)"
"4341","The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone says when swearing an oath: ""If Allah wills,"" he makes an exception. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3261)"
"4342","The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone swears an oath and makes an exception, he may fulfil it if he wishes and break it if he wishes without any accountability for breaking. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3262)"
"4343","I will surely fight against the Quraysh. By Allah! I will surely fight against the Quraysh. By Allah! I will surely fight against the Quraysh."" Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent for a while, then he said: ""If Allah wills."
"4344","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever swears an oath regarding his slave that he will beat him, then its expiation is that he abandons this act, and along with the expiation, this is also a good deed."
"4345","He who took an oath, but he found something else better than that, should do that which is better and break his oath. (Using translation from Muslim 1651b)"
"4346","The man was not satisfied with this, so Sayyiduna ‘Adi (may Allah be pleased with him) swore that he would not give him anything. Then the man agreed to this, so Sayyiduna ‘Adi (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If I had not heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this: “Whoever takes an oath and then sees that something else is closer to piety with Allah, then he should do that which is more pious,” (Sayyiduna ‘Adi (may Allah be pleased with him) says: If this hadith had not been there) I would not have broken my oath."
"4347","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: ""Whoever swears an oath then sees that something else is better than it, let him do that which is better and offer expiation for what he swore about. "" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2108)"
"4348","The Prophet Muhammad said: ""O Abdur Rahman! Do not ask for a government position, because if it is given to you as a result of your asking, you will be left to it (without divine help), but if it is given to you without your asking, you will be helped in it. And when you take an oath regarding something and later find that something else is better than it, then do what is better and offer expiation for your oath."
"4349","""Whoever swears an oath, then sees something better than it, let him do that which is better."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3781)"
"4350","There came to our house some guests. It was a common practice with my father to (go) and talk to Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the night. While going he said: 'Abd al-Rahman, entertain the guests. When it was evening we served the food to them, but they refused saying: So long as the owner of the house does not come and join us, we would not take the meal. I said to them: He ('Abd Bakr) is a stern person, and if you would not do that (if you do not take the food). I fear, I may be harmed by him, but they refused. As he (my father) came, the first thing he asked was: Have you served the guests? They (the peopleof the household) said: We have not served them sofar. He said: Did I not command 'Abd al-Rahman (to do this)? He ('Abd al-Rahman) said: I slunk away and kept myself away by that time. He again said: O stupid fellow, I ask you on oath that In case you hear my voice you come to me. I came and said: By Allah, there is no fault of mine. These are your guests; you may ask them. I provided them with food but they refused to eat until you came. He said to them: Why is it that you did not accept our food? By Allah, I shall not even take food tonight (as you have not taken). They said: By Allah, we would not take until you join us. Thereupon he Abu Bakr) said: I have never seen a more unfortunate night than this. Woe be to thee! that you do not accept from us food prepared for you. He again said: What I did first (that is the taking of vow for not eating the food) was prompted by the Satan. Bring the food. The food was brought, and he ate by reciting the name of Allah and they also ate, and when it was morning he came to Allah's Apostle ﷺ and said: Messenger of Allah, their oath (that of the guests) came to be true, but mine was not true, and after that he informed him of the whole incident. He said: Your oath came to be the most true and you are the best of them. He (the narrator) said. I do not know whether he made an atonement for it. (Using translation from Muslim 2057b)"
"4351","I will not provide riding animals for those people. Then some camels were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he had them separated; fifteen camels remained. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Where is Abdullah bin Qais? They replied: He is here. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Take them and have your people ride on them. He said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! You had sworn (that you would not give us riding animals). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Even though I had sworn (still, you take them)."
"4352","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: ""Whoever swears an oath then sees that something else is better than it, let him do that which is better and offer expiation for what he swore about. "" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2108)"
"4353","I take an oath and I consider another course of action to be better, I will do what is better and offer expiation for my oath."
"4354","I will not give you animals for riding. (The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) By Allah! I will not give you animals for riding. The narrator says: When we returned to our place of residence (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) when we started returning to our place of residence, at that time some camels were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent three white-humped camels from among them to us. One of us said to another: Should we ride on them when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has already sworn (that he will not give us camels for riding)? So we went to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! You have taken an oath. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: By Allah! I did not give you camels for riding, rather Allah Almighty has given you animals for riding. Whenever I take an oath about something on the face of the earth and then I see a situation better than that, I will do that which is better. (About one word here, the narrator is in doubt.)"
"4355","There were two brothers among the Ansar who shared an inheritance. When one of them asked the other for the portion due to him, he replied: If you ask me again for the portion due to you, all my property will be devoted to the decoration of the Ka'bah. Umar said to him: The Ka'bah does not need your property. Make atonement for your oath and speak to your brother. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: An oath or vow to disobey the Lord, or to break ties of relationship or about something over which one has no control is not binding on you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3272)"
"4356","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""An oath (leads to) either sin or regret. "" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2103)"
"4357","The Prophet ﷺ said: Do not swear by your fathers, or by your mothers, or by rivals to Allah; and swear by Allah only, and swear by Allah only when you are speaking the truth. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3248)"
"4358","Ibn Umar heard a man swearing: No, I swear by the Ka'bah. Ibn Umar said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: He who swears by anyone but Allah is polytheist. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3251)"
"4359","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ found 'Umar al-Khattab in a caravan while he was swearing by his father. So he said: Allah forbids you to swear by forefathers. If anyone swears, he must swear by Allah or keep silence. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3249)"
"4360","Messenger of Allah ﷺ met ʿUmar bin Al-Khattab while the latter was going with a group of camel-riders, and he was swearing by his father. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Lo! Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers, so whoever has to take an oath, he should swear by Allah or keep quiet."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6646)"
"4361","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ found 'Umar al-Khattab in a caravan while he was swearing by his father. So he said: Allah forbids you to swear by forefathers. If anyone swears, he must swear by Allah or keep silence. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3249)"
"4362","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears, let him not swear by anything other than Allah.'"" The Quraish used to swear by their forefathers, and so he said: ""Do not swear by your forefathers."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3764)"
"4363","The narrator named Ibn Buraidah is Abdullah bin Buraidah bin Husaib."
"4364","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Say three times, ""There is no deity except Allah, He is the only One worthy of worship."" Then spit three times to your left and seek Allah's protection from the accursed Satan, and do not do this again."
"4365","The time of ignorance is still near, and I (mistakenly) swore by Lat and 'Uzza. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said to me: Recite this three times, ""There is no deity except Allah, He alone is the only deity."" Spit to your left three times, blow, and seek refuge with Allah from Satan, and do not do this again."
"4366","Verily the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who took an oath on a religion other than Islam as a liar would become so as he said, and he who slaughtered himself with a thing would be slaughtered with that on the Day of Resurrection. (Using translation from Muslim 110d)"
"4367","""Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, telling a lie, will be as he said, and whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it in the Hereafter."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3771)"
"4368","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever swears a false oath upon this pulpit of mine, he makes his abode in the Hellfire."
"4369","Sayyiduna Qais bin ‘Asim (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about making an ally (according to the custom of the pre-Islamic era): so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There is no making of an ally (in this manner) in Islam."
"4370","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There is no alliance in Islam, and Islam strengthened the alliance made during pre-Islamic days. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2925)"
"4371","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There is no alliance in Islam, and Islam strengthened the alliance made during pre-Islamic days. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2925)"
"4372","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There is no alliance in Islam, and Islam strengthened the alliance made during pre-Islamic days. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2925)"
"4373","I participated with my uncle in the alliance of 'Mutayyibeen', and I would not like to break that alliance even if I were given red camels in exchange."
"4374","I did not participate in any pact of the Quraysh except the pact of 'Mutayyibeen', and I do not wish to break this pact even if I were to be given red camels in exchange for it."" (The narrator states:) By 'Mutayyibeen' is meant Banu Hashim, Banu Umayyah, Banu Zuhrah, and Banu Makhzum. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In both narrations, it is mentioned that I participated in the pact of 'Mutayyibeen', whereas the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not participate in the pact of 'Mutayyibeen' because the pact of 'Mutayyibeen' took place before the birth of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) participated in the pact of 'Hilf al-Fudul', and this too took place among the 'Mutayyibeen'. I have discussed this narration in detail in my book ""Al-Tawreeh wal-Hajb""."
"4375","By Allah, I am certain that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that. (Using translation from Aḥmad 101)"
"4376","""Do not make vows, for a vow does not have any impact on the Qadar. Rather it is just a means of taking wealth from the miserly."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3805)"
"4377","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A vow does not bring anything to an end; through it, wealth is taken out from a miser."
"4378","The man said to him: I had vowed that my son would go on foot, but my son has passed away. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) became angry and said: Were you not forbidden from making vows? I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Indeed, a vow does not bring anything forward or delay it, but Allah, through it, extracts wealth from the miser."" (The narrator says) When I saw this situation, I said to that man: Go to Saeed bin Musayyib and ask him about this issue. He went to him and asked about this issue. Then he returned, so I asked: What answer did he give you? He said: He told me: Go on foot on behalf of your son. He asked: Is this permissible for me? So Saeed bin Musayyib said: What do you think, if your son had a debt and you paid it off, would it be considered paid on his behalf? I replied: Yes. So he said: Go on foot on behalf of your son."
"4379","O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I vowed during the jahiliyyah to observe i’tikaf for one night in al-Masjid al-Haram. He said to him: “Fulfil your vow.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 255)"
"4380","O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I vowed during the jahiliyyah to observe i’tikaf for one night in al-Masjid al-Haram. He said to him: “Fulfil your vow.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 255)"
"4381","I lodged her in the houses of the villagers until, when I camped, some captives of Hunayn came before me who had run out and were saying: The Messenger of Allah has set us free. So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): Go and set that slave girl free. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: So I went and I set her free. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In the wording of the narration, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) has clarified that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had made a vow to perform i'tikaf for one night, and this is mentioned only in this narration, because the wording of this narration is: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had made a vow to perform i'tikaf for one day. So if these words are authentically established, then it is possible that by ""day"" here it is meant: to perform i'tikaf along with the night of that day, and where the word ""night"" is used, it means that its day will be included. In this way, there will remain no contradiction between the two narrations."
"4382","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a man who was walking with the support of two people between him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) inquired about him. So the people informed: He has made a vow that he will go on foot (the narrator says: that is, he will go on foot to the Ka'bah). So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah, the Exalted, is free from need of this person putting himself in hardship. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed that man to ride. Layth, Haql, and Awza'i all belong to the same era. Abdur Rahman bin Yaman, Yahya bin Sa'id, and Humaid belong to one era; they have narrated from each other. This has been stated by the Shaykh."
"4383","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a man who was walking with the support of two people between him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) inquired: What is the matter with him? The people informed: He has vowed to perform Hajj on foot. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah is not in need of his walking; he should ride."
"4384","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Tell her to ride and give expiation. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) There is a possibility that this woman either swore an oath or made a vow to go for Hajj on foot; however, there is no expiation in a vow."
"4385","While the Prophet ﷺ was preaching a man was standing in the sun. He asked about him. They said: He is Abu Isra'il who has taken a vow to stand and not to sit, or go into shade, or speak, but to fast. Thereupon he said: Command him to speak, to go into the shade, sit and complete his fast. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3300)"
"4386","I had vowed that if Allah brought you back safely, I would beat the drum (duff) near you."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""If you had made a vow, then do so; otherwise, do not."" She said, ""I had made a vow,"" so the Prophet (peace be upon him) sat down and she beat the drum."
"4387","""Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3806)"
"4388","""Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3806)"
"4389","""Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3806)"
"4390","""Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3806)"
"4391","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""A vow regarding a sin should not be fulfilled, nor should a vow be fulfilled regarding something over which a servant has no control (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) over which the son of Adam has no control."
"4392","The narrator states: So the woman was saved, she came to Madinah Munawwarah, and then she began to sacrifice the she-camel. The people stopped her from doing so. This matter was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You have given it a very bad reward. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is not obligatory for a person to fulfill a vow that involves sin, or that concerns something which he does not own."
"4393","Sa'd b. 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: My Mother has died and she could not fulfill her vow which she had taken. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Fulfill it on her behalf. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3307)"
"4394","""Fulfill it on her behalf."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3817)"
"4395","Sa'd bin 'Ubadah came to the Prophet and said: ""My mother has died and she had a vow to fulfill but she did not do so."" He said: ""Fulfill it on her behalf."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3663)"
"4396","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to this woman: Would you pay off the debt of your mother if it was obligatory upon her? The woman replied: Yes. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Then you should also fast on behalf of your mother."
"4397","""Abu Hurairah said: 'Carrying out a Hadd punishment in a land is better for its people than if it were to rain for forty nights."" (Daif) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4905)"
"4398","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Establishing a prescribed punishment (hadd) on the earth is better than forty days of rainfall."
"4399","A man of the tribe of Aslam came to the Prophet ﷺ and testified four times against himself that he had had illicit intercourse with a woman, while all the time the Prophet ﷺ was turning away from him. Then when he confessed a fifth time, he turned round and asked: Did you have intercourse with her? He replied: Yes. He asked: Have you done it so that your sexual organ penetrated hers? He replied: Yes. He asked: Have you done it like a collyrium stick when enclosed in its case and a rope in a well? He replied: Yes. He asked: Do you know what fornication is? He replied: Yes. I have done with her unlawfully what a man may lawfully do with his wife. He then asked: What do you want from what you have said? He said: I want you to purify me. So he gave orders regarding him and he was stoned to death. Then the Prophet ﷺ heard one of his companions saying to another: Look at this man whose fault was concealed by Allah but who would not leave the matter alone, so that he was stoned like a dog. He said nothing to them but walked on for a time till he came to the corpse of an ass with its legs in the air. He asked: Where are so and so? They said: Here we are, Messenger of Allah ﷺ! He said: Go down and eat some of this ass's corpse. They replied: Messenger of Allah! Who can eat any of this? He said: The dishonour you have just shown to your brother is more serious than eating some of it. By Him in Whose hand my soul is, he is now among the rivers of Paradise and plunging into them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4428)"
"4400","I have done with a woman unlawfully the same act that a man does with his wife. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered regarding him, so he was sent away from there. He came a fourth time to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! The man from afar has committed adultery. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Woe to you, do you know what adultery is? Did you enter and withdraw? He replied: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered regarding him that he be stoned. When stones began to hit him, he took shelter behind a tree, then he was stoned to death at that tree until he died. After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was passing by, accompanied by some of his companions. One of them said to his companion: By your father, this man is doomed to loss; he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) several times, and each time the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent him back, until he was killed in such a way as a dog is killed. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent regarding both of them until he passed by the carcass of a donkey whose leg was raised upwards. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Eat from it, both of you. They said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Should we eat the carcass of a donkey? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The attack you made on your brother's honor is a greater sin than this. By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, that man is now diving in the rivers of Paradise."
"4401","I have seen him swimming in the rivers of Paradise."
"4402","The Quraish were anxious about the Makhzumi woman who had committed theft, They said : Who will speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about her ? Then they said: Who will be bold enough for it but Uasmah bin Zaid, the prophet’s ﷺ friend! So Usamah spoke to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said : Are you interceding regarding one of the punishments prescribed by Allah ? He then got up and gave an address, saying : What destroyed your predecessors was just that when a person of rank among them committed a theft, They left him alone , and when a weak one of them committed a theft, they inflicted the prescribed punishment on him . I swear by Allah that if Fatimah daughter of Muhammad should steal, I would have her hand cut off. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4373)"
"4403","a woman from Juhainah came to the Messenger of Allah sand said: ""I have committed Zina."" And she was committed Zina."" And She was pregnant. He handed her over to her guardian and said: ""Look after her, and when she gave birth, he brought her to him. He ordered that her garment be wrapped around her, then he offered the funeral prayer for her. 'Umar said to him: ""Are you praying for her even though she committed Zina?"" he said: ""She has repented in a manner that, if it were to be shared among seventy of the people of Al-Madinah it would suffice them. Have you ever seen repentance better than the one who sacrificed herself for the sake of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime?"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1957)"
"4404","al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stoned Ma'iz ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: ""I saw him splashing about in the rivers of Paradise."""
"4405","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) took the pledge from us in the same manner as he took from our women. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Whoever among you commits any act that is liable to a prescribed punishment and is punished for it in this world, then that punishment will be an expiation for him. And whoever's matter is deferred (i.e., he is not punished in this world), then his case is with Allah Almighty; if He wills, He will have mercy on him, and if He wills, He will punish him."
"4406","I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Different evils will make their appearance in the near future. Anyone who tries to disrupt the affairs of this Umma while they are united you should strike him with the sword whoever he be. (If remonstrance does not prevail with him and he does not desist from his disruptive activities, he is to be killed.) (Using translation from Muslim 1852a)"
"4407","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “By the One besides whom there is no deity, it is not permissible to kill any person who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, except in three cases: a person who abandons Islam and separates from the (Muslim) community, a married adulterer, and a person who is killed in retaliation for (murdering) another.” A’mash states: I narrated this hadith to Ibrahim, so he narrated to me a similar narration from Aswad, from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"4408","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""It is not permissible to shed the blood of a person who testifies that there is no deity except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, except in three cases: a married adulterer, a life for a life, and a person who abandons his religion (i.e., Islam) and separates from the community (i.e., such a person is to be killed).\"""""
"4409","That Sa'd b. 'Ubadah said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ : What do you think if I find with my wife a man ; should I give him some time until I bring four witnesses ?"" He said: ""Yes"". (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4533)"
"4410","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When adultery and usury become widespread among a people, they make Allah's punishment lawful for themselves."
"4411","Do you know who is poor? They (the Companions of the Holy Prophet) said: A poor man amongst us is one who has neither dirham with him nor wealth. He (the Holy Prophet) said: The poor of my Umma would be he who would come on the Day of Resurrection with prayers and fasts and Zakat but (he would find himself bankrupt on that day as he would have exhausted his funds of virtues) since he hurled abuses upon others, brought calumny against others and unlawfully consumed the wealth of others and shed the blood of others and beat others, and his virtues would be credited to the account of one (who suffered at his hand). And if his good deeds fall short to clear the account, then his sins would be entered in (his account) and he would be thrown in the Hell-Fire. (Using translation from Muslim 2581)"
"4412","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""The one who commits an illegal sexual intercourse is not a believer at the time of committing illegal sexual intercourse and a thief is not a believer at the time of committing theft and a drinker of alcoholic drink is not a believer at the time of drinking. Yet, (the gate of) repentance is open thereafter."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6810)"
"4413","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""There are three people whom Allah Almighty will not look at with mercy on the Day of Resurrection: an old adulterer, a lying ruler, and a poor arrogant person."
"4414","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That you associate a partner with Allah, while He (Allah) created you. (The questioner) asked: Then which one? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That you commit adultery with your neighbor’s wife. (The narrator states) So Allah Almighty revealed this verse in confirmation of it: ""And those who do not worship anyone along with Allah, and do not kill any soul whom Allah has forbidden (to kill), except by right, and do not commit adultery. Whoever does this shall meet the penalty of sin."
"4415","I asked the Prophet, ""What is the greatest sin in the Sight of Allah?"" He said, ""That you set up a rival unto Allah though He Alone created you."" I said, ""That is indeed a great sin."" Then asked, ""What is next?"" He said, ""To kill your son lest he should share your food with you."" I asked, ""What is next?"" He said, ""To commit illegal sexual intercourse with the wife of your neighbor."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 4477)"
"4416","‘Abd Allaah (bin Masud) said “I asked Apostle of Allaah ﷺ which sin is the gravest?” He replied “That you associate someone with Allaah, while He has created you”. I again asked “Which then?” He replied “That you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbor.” Allaah then revealed the following Qur’anic verse in support of the statement of the Prophet ﷺ “Those who invoke not with Allaah any other god nor slay such life as Allaah has made sacred except for just cause nor commit fornication.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2310)"
"4417","The narrator states) Regarding the act of the people of Lut, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this three times. The narrator named Abdul Malik is Abu Amir Uqdi."
"4418","“Allah will not look at a man who enters a man or a woman in the behind.” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1165)"
"4419","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Both eyes commit adultery, the tongue commits adultery, both hands commit adultery, both feet commit adultery, and the private part either confirms it or denies it."
"4420","I have not seen anything that resembles sin more than what Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) has narrated, that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has written the share of adultery for the son of Adam, which he will inevitably reach. So the adultery of the eye is looking, the adultery of the tongue is speaking, and the soul desires and wishes, and the private part either confirms it or denies it."
"4421","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every human being has his share of adultery, which he will inevitably reach. The adultery of the eye is looking, the adultery of the tongue is speaking, the adultery of the heart is desiring, and the private part either confirms or denies it."
"4422","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Every human being inevitably commits adultery; the adultery of the eye is looking, the adultery of the hand is touching, the soul desires, and the private part either confirms or denies it."
"4423","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""A share of adultery has been decreed for every human being. The adultery of the eye is looking, the adultery of the ear is listening, the adultery of the hand is touching, the adultery of the feet is walking (towards it), the adultery of the tongue is speaking, and the heart desires and wishes, and the private parts either confirm or deny it.\"""""
"4424","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""Any woman who applies perfume and passes by people so that they may smell her fragrance, then she is an adulteress, and every eye (that looks at her) is an adulterous eye.\"""""
"4425","Receive my teachings, receive my teachings. Allah has appointed a way for those women. If the parties have been married, they shall receive a hundred lashes and stoned to death. If the parties are unmarried, they shall receive a hundred lashes and banished for a year. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4415)"
"4426","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Take from me. For Allah has a way made for them : For the married person who commits adultery with a married person is one hundred lashes, then stoning. And for the virgin who commits adultery with a virgin is one hundred lashes and banishment for a year."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1434)"
"4427","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Take the rulings from me. Allah Almighty has clarified the command for them. If an unmarried person commits (zina) with an unmarried person, and a married person commits (zina) with a married person, then the unmarried shall be flogged and exiled for one year, and the married shall be flogged and stoned."
"4428","Sūrat al-Aḥzāb was equivalent ˹in size˺ to Sūrat al-Baqarah and there was ˹an Āyah˺ in it: ""al-shaykhu wa-al-shaykhah idhā zanayā fārjumūhumā al-battata (The ˹married˺ man and a woman, if they commit adultery, then absolutely stone them.)"""
"4429","The narrator says, so I replied: Seventy-three verses. Sayyiduna Ubayy (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By the One in whose name oaths are sworn, it was as long as Surah Al-Baqarah, and we used to recite in it verses regarding the ruling of stoning. In it was this command: If a married man commits adultery with a married woman, then you must certainly stone them both. This is a punishment from Allah Almighty. Allah is Mighty and Wise."
"4430","narrates: Whoever denies the punishment of stoning has denied the Most Merciful, and Allah Almighty has said: ""O People of the Book! Our Messenger has come to you, clarifying to you much of what you used to hide from the Book, and overlooking much."" (Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates) So among the things they used to hide was the punishment of stoning."
"4431","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had two Jews (a man and a woman) stoned who were muhsan (married)."
"4432","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had two married Jews (a man and a woman) stoned to death."
"4433","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had a Jewish man and a Jewish woman stoned to death."
"4434","some jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned to him that a man and a women of their number had committed fornication. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them: What do you find in the Torah about stoning? They replied: We disgrace them and they should be flogged. ‘Abd Allah b. Salam said: You lie; it contains (instruction for) stoning. So they brought the Torah and spread it out, and one of them put his hand over the verse of stoning and read what preceded it and what followed it. ‘Abd Allah b. Salam said to him: Lift your hand. When he did so, the verse of stoning was seen to be in it. They then said: He has spoken the truth, Muhammad, the verse of stoning is in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then gave command regarding them, and they were stoned to death. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Umar said: I saw the man leaning on the woman protecting her from the stones. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4446)"
"4435","some jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned to him that a man and a women of their number had committed fornication. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them: What do you find in the Torah about stoning? They replied: We disgrace them and they should be flogged. ‘Abd Allah b. Salam said: You lie; it contains (instruction for) stoning. So they brought the Torah and spread it out, and one of them put his hand over the verse of stoning and read what preceded it and what followed it. ‘Abd Allah b. Salam said to him: Lift your hand. When he did so, the verse of stoning was seen to be in it. They then said: He has spoken the truth, Muhammad, the verse of stoning is in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then gave command regarding them, and they were stoned to death. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Umar said: I saw the man leaning on the woman protecting her from the stones. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4446)"
"4436","I will make him an example for others."" The narrator named Simak sometimes narrated a word differently. The narrator named Simak states: I narrated this tradition before Sa'id bin Jubair, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent that person back four times. The narrator named Shu'bah states, the narrator named Hakam narrated this, and it is appropriate that such a person be sent back four times. Whereas the narrator named Hammad mentioned that he should be sent back once."
"4437","A bedouin came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Allah's apostle! I ask you by Allah to judge My case according to Allah's Laws."" His opponent, who was more learned than he, said, ""Yes, judge between us according to Allah's Laws, and allow me to speak."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Speak."" He (i .e. the bedouin or the other man) said, ""My son was working as a laborer for this (man) and he committed illegal sexual intercourse with his wife. The people told me that it was obligatory that my son should be stoned to death, so in lieu of that I ransomed my son by paying one hundred sheep and a slave girl. Then I asked the religious scholars about it, and they informed me that my son must be lashed one hundred lashes, and be exiled for one year, and the wife of this (man) must be stoned to death."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""By Him in Whose Hands my soul is, I will judge between you according to Allah's Laws. The slave-girl and the sheep are to be returned to you, your son is to receive a hundred lashes and be exiled for one year. You, Unais, go to the wife of this (man) and if she confesses her guilt, stone her to death."" Unais went to that woman next morning and she confessed. Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that she be stoned to death. (Using translation from Bukhārī 2724)"
"4438","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) sent him back several times. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked the people of his tribe: Does he have any illness? It was said that he has no illness, but his condition is such that he believes the only expiation for the crime he has committed is that the prescribed punishment be carried out on him. The narrator states: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) ordered us, so we took him towards Baqi’ Gharqad. The narrator states: We did not dig any pit for him, nor did we tie him up. We started stoning him with stones, bones, and clods of earth. The narrator says: When he was hurt, he ran away and we also ran after him, until he stopped near a stony ground. We continued to stone him until he died. In the evening, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) stood up to deliver a sermon. After praising and glorifying Allah, he said: As for what follows! ""What is wrong with people that when we go out to participate in a battle, one of them stays behind with our families and, like a male animal, tries to attract (a woman) by making sounds? It is incumbent upon me that if any such person is brought to me, I will give him an exemplary punishment."" The narrator says: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) neither spoke ill of that person nor prayed for his forgiveness."
"4439","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned away from him. Then he came from another side to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: I have committed adultery. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned away from him. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) four times, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that he be stoned. When stones struck him, he ran away. People mentioned his running away to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that when stones struck him (he ran away), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Why did you not leave him?"
